# Optional root-owned configuration: the owner TDX measurement allowlist.
#
# The validator reads CATHEDRAL_TDX_MEASUREMENT_POLICY from its environment,
# not from a flag, so a runtime from before this setting ignores it: an update
# rollback never meets an argument it rejects. Unset or empty means no policy,
# exactly as before.
#
# The policy file is strict JSON, root or operator owned and not group or world
# writable, like the SNP policy:
#
#   {"schema": "cathedral_tdx_measurement_policy_v1",
#    "mode": "shadow",
#    "allowed_measurements": ["tdx-measurement-sha256:<64 hex>", ...]}
#
# Generate it, and its <policy>.source.json record of the signed list release,
# with cathedral-sandbox's "cathedral policy-registry export-measurement-policy"
# (README, "Optional: TDX measurement allowlist"). Install both with the
# service group able to read them:
#   sudo install -o root -g cathedral-validator -m 0440 policy.json \
#     /etc/cathedral-validator/tdx-measurement-policy.json
#   sudo install -o root -g cathedral-validator -m 0440 policy.json.source.json \
#     /etc/cathedral-validator/tdx-measurement-policy.json.source.json
#
# "shadow" records each machine's measurement and whether it is allowed, and
# pays as before; each cycle's service-log line lists what it saw under
# evidence_summary.tdx_measurement. "enforce" pays only listed measurements.
# Start in shadow, review and list those measurements, then enforce.
#
# Both files are read once, at start: restart cathedral-validator-direct after
# editing either. The unit from bootstrap sequence 3 does not read this file;
# add the drop-in in docs/AUTO_UPDATE.md ("Optional unit settings") until a
# newer bootstrap is installed. The service log says "LOADED" at start when a
# policy applies, with the signed release its source record names, and
# "NOT_LOADED" when this file exists but is not read.
CATHEDRAL_TDX_MEASUREMENT_POLICY=/etc/cathedral-validator/tdx-measurement-policy.json
